{
  "quest.551695798DCC9F60.quest_desc": [
    "On top on self-repairing during an &bAurora&r, each piece also has unique abilities which can be seen in their item tooltips.",
  ],
  "quest.7694FA3E97015D23.quest_desc": [
    "Magical flowers that appear on snow during an aurora and grow through &afour stages&r. Anything left behind wilts at sunrise.",
    "",
    "They spawn on snow layers, snow blocks, powder snow, ice, packed ice, blue ice and &bShimmering Ice&r.",
    "",
    "Breaking a fully grown one drops &dFrozen Petals&r (1-4 with Fortune) plus the living bloom itself, so you can replant it somewhere safer.",
    "",
    "A bloom placed on a snow layer or in powder snow remembers which it was, and restores it when broken.",
  ],
  "quest.2EFFDC001A3BCFBD.title": "&fThe Shimmer Spear",
  "quest.4E326D6986822470.quest_desc": [
    "&dFrozen Petals&r are the key to everything else.",
    "",
    "Harvest them from &aAurora Blooms&r that spawn on snow during an aurora.",
    "",
    "&7&oGet a decent stack. Petals feed the basin, the brewing stand and the seeds.&r",
  ],
  "quest.6DD4902A109331D3.quest_desc": [
    "Sneak + Right-Click any snow surface with &aboth hands empty&r and you leave an imprint behind.",
    "",
    "They fade after five minutes on their own. Right-click one with a &dFrozen Petal&r to keep it forever.",
    "",
    "&7&oPurely for fun, which is rather the point.&r",
  ],
  "quest.6795EDD4CF4B5A1D.quest_desc": [
    "Light level &a15&r, cycles gently through green, blue and pink, works underwater, and hangs from floors, walls or ceilings.",
    "",
    "&cHeld in either hand it grants immunity to the Darkness effect.",
    "",
    "Which makes it exactly what you want in the Deep Dark, and against the Warden.",
  ],
  "quest.192DD755D7D0C4C8.quest_desc": [
    "&aGlow Leek Seeds&r are the first crop the aurora unlocks, and the cheapest use for spare &dFrozen Petals&r.",
    "",
    "They will only grow on &bShimmering Ice&r, need no light at all, and keep growing through the night.",
    "",
    "Eating one grants &aNight Vision&r and &2Glowing&r. The &aCandied&r version drops the glowing and keeps the night vision, which is usually what you want.",
  ],
  "quest.6A1048464ABAA02B.quest_desc": [
    "Craft &aUnrefined Shimmersteel&r, then infuse it in a &bGlacial Basin&r.",
    "",
    "&cThe basin has to be completely full&r, and the infusion consumes all three levels of Liquid Aura at once.",
    "",
    "Shimmersteel sits slightly above iron and below diamond, but it has &ahigh enchantability&r and &2Aurora Affinity&r. Every Shimmersteel and Shimmerweave piece repairs itself while equipped during an aurora.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "A &fShimmersteel Ingot&f works as an armor trim material, giving any piece an icy blue gradient that shifts between blue and silver.",
    "",
    "It works with every vanilla armor type and every vanilla trim pattern, and with most modded armor that supports the trim system.",
  ],
  "quest.120CAE5492D8D2FE.title": "&dAurora Events",
  "task.223B391ADCC0E276.title": "Any Shimmersteel Tool",
  "quest.0A25BE050F85F9D1.title": "&fShimmersteel Tools",
  "quest.780B8C00D01127EB.title": "&bAuroral",
  "quest.0A25BE050F85F9D1.quest_desc": [
    "Five tools, each with its own trick, all upgraded from iron at a &aSmithing Table&r with the &2Shimmersteel Upgrade Template&r.",
    "",
    "- &aPickaxe&r has inherent &bFortune III&r on vanilla diamond, emerald, lapis, redstone and nether quartz ores, and on amethyst. Modded gem ores do not get it.",
    "- &2Shovel&r has inherent &bSilk Touch&r.",
    "- &aHoe&r has Silk Touch too, and creates &bShimmer Soil&r.",
    "- &2Axe&r force-oxidizes copper on right-click.",
    "- &aSword&r applies &bFrostbite&r, executes below &c15%&r health, and leaves a snow layer where the target falls.",
    "",
    "The pickaxe alone is worth the trip. Fortune III with no enchanting.",
  ],
  "quest.096D4B6971E6F817.quest_desc": [
    "Infuse &aWoven Leather&r in a &bGlacial Basin&r and you get &2Shimmerweave Fabric&r. It only costs one level of aura, so it is far cheaper than an ingot.",
    "",
    "Only Woven Leather works. Plain Leather and Wool do nothing in the basin, so craft the Woven Leather first.",
    "",
    "Every Shimmerweave piece is an iron armor piece upgraded at a Smithing Table with the &aShimmersteel Upgrade Template&r and fabric, and every piece repairs itself during an aurora.",
  ],
  "quest.4E42490104D43551.quest_desc": [
    "It fires &asnowballs&r, not arrows, and turns each one into a &bStar-Shot&r.",
    "",
    "Star-Shots do more damage than arrows, leave a light trail, and &aflashbang&r everything near the impact. They cannot be picked up again, but you are in a cold biome and snowballs are everywhere.",
  ],
  "quest.6DD4902A109331D3.title": "&fSnow Angels",
  "quest.427563F5E92CA507.quest_desc": [
    "Ender Blooms never spawn naturally. Right-click an &aAurora Bloom&r with an &5Ender Pearl&r and it converts at the same growth stage.",
    "",
    "Unlike ordinary blooms they &apersist forever&r, with no wilting at sunrise and no vanishing when the aurora ends. They only advance stages on &bShimmer Soil&r or &5End Stone&r.",
    "",
    "A mature one drops an &5Aurora Ender Shard&r and has a &a5%&r chance of an extra bloom. &3Two shards craft back into an Ender Pearl&r.",
    "",
    "That makes Ender Pearls renewable without a single Enderman.",
  ],
  "task.6E0621EE142B45DE.title": "&bThe Auroral Nautilus",
  "quest.4553492B0110AC64.quest_desc": [
    "A peaceful creature that floats through the sky in circles, only during auroras, and fades away gracefully half a minute after the lights go out.",
    "",
    "Wild ones drift toward anyone holding an &dAurora Shard&r. Feed one a shard and there is a &b33% chance&r per shard to tame it. Once tamed it stops despawning and orbits you.",
    "",
    "- &aSneak + Right-click&r toggles Follow and Stay.",
    "- &2Right-click&r to ride, no saddle needed.",
    "[\"\", \"- \", {\"text\": \"Hold \", \"color\": \"green\"}, {\"keybind\": \"key.jump\", \"color\": \"yellow\", \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Default: Space\"}}, \" to charge, then release for up to a \", {\"text\": \"3x\", \"color\": \"green\"}, \" speed boost.\"]",
    "",
    "It comes in three sizes, and it can be given armor.",
  ],
  "quest.0B7E9D8A24F07AF5.title": "&bShimmering Ice",
  "quest.0B7E9D8A24F07AF5.quest_desc": [
    "Aurora-infused ice that never melts, glows at light level &a8&r, and hydrates farmland within &a4 blocks&r just like water.",
    "",
    "Infuse ordinary &aIce&r in a &bGlacial Basin&r. It never generates in the world, so the basin is the only source.",
    "",
    "Pair it with &bShimmer Soil&r, made by right-clicking snow or dirt with the &2Shimmersteel Hoe&r. Crops on Shimmer Soil grow 3x faster at night and 5x faster during an aurora, with no water channels and no extra lighting.",
    "",
    "The glow is enough to stop mobs spawning, which makes this ideal underground.",
  ],
  "quest.551695798DCC9F60.title": "&6Shimmerweave Armor",
  "quest.40420EB20069A628.quest_desc": [
    "Hearthwood Logs do not generate anywhere in the world, so craft one. Light it with &aFlint and Steel&r.",
    "",
    "A lit log burns for &a7 in-game days&r of chunk-loaded time and does four things at once:",
    "",
    "- &aFrostbite Immunity&r within 16 blocks.",
    "- &2Repels Phantoms&r and ignites the ones that come anyway.",
    "- &aImproves villager trades&r.",
    "- &2Aurora Catalyst&r: +15% aurora chance per lit log within 32 blocks, up to +45% for three, which pushes a night to roughly 78%.",
    "",
    "Keep three lit where you sleep and you will rarely miss an aurora. It is a strong boost, not a guarantee.",
  ],
  "quest.455141615CF5D0FC.quest_desc": [
    "A brewing stand that burns &asnowballs&r instead of Blaze Powder. Each snowball fuels ten brews.",
    "",
    "&dFrozen Petals&r brew an &aAwkward Potion&r from a Water Bottle exactly like Nether Wart does, and that works in an ordinary Brewing Stand too.",
    "",
    "Between the two, the whole potion tree opens up without setting foot in the Nether.",
  ],
  "quest.4E326D6986822470.title": "&dFirst Steps",
  "quest.5CE6320CF1FED392.title": "&6Food and Drink",
  "quest.780B8C00D01127EB.quest_desc": [
    "&7&o\"The sky gives, the ice remembers.\"&r",
    "",
    "&eAuroral&r turns cold biomes from barren wastes into a whole progression line, built around the &aAurora Borealis&r.",
    "",
    "The loop is short. Wait for an aurora, harvest &dFrozen Petals&r, build a &bGlacial Basin&r, collect &bLiquid Aura&r, and infuse it into &fShimmersteel&f and &fShimmerweave&f.",
    "",
    "&7&oThe Auroral Guidebook covers all of this in far more depth. This chapter follows its chapters in order.&r",
  ],
  "quest.38EF63D7153D6AC5.title": "&bThe Glacial Basin",
  "quest.5CE6320CF1FED392.quest_desc": [
    "Cold-biome snacks. None of them need the &bCold Brewing Stand&r, since they all come from a Crafting Table, a furnace or a campfire.",
    "",
    "- &aHot Cocoa&r gives 5 minutes of Frostbite immunity and 30 seconds of Regeneration.",
    "- &2Frosted Cookies&r are a sweet treat with a shimmer to them.",
    "- &aRoasted Snowball&r is a toasted snowball, and deeply offensive to a Nautilus.",
    "- &2Sugared Roasted Snowball&r is the apology a Nautilus will accept.",
  ],
  "quest.761D8E1A5322E1CB.quest_desc": [
    "Eating one gives &b30 seconds&r of &bConduit Power&r, so you can breathe and see underwater, and it resets the Phantom timer as if you had slept.",
    "",
    "Keep one for an underwater trip or a long night away from a bed.",
  ],
  "quest.2EFFDC001A3BCFBD.quest_desc": [
    "Long reach, piercing damage, and a charged stab on right-click. It wants a full-cooldown commitment. Partial swings hit noticeably softer.",
    "",
    "Every hit applies &bFrostbite I&r for 5 seconds. Frostbite slows the target, lowers its armor, cuts its healing and wears its shield down faster. Another hit refreshes it rather than stacking it.",
    "",
    "&aDuring an aurora&r each hit deals 2 extra damage and applies &bFrostbite II&r for 10 seconds instead.",
    "",
    "It pairs well with the &aShimmerweave Skates&r for fighting on ice.",
  ],
  "quest.192DD755D7D0C4C8.title": "&aGlow Leeks",
  "quest.734BB52B2E3B94D5.title": "&bThe Auroral Snowlette",
  "quest.6795EDD4CF4B5A1D.title": "&bThe Aurora Lantern",
  "quest.40420EB20069A628.title": "&6The Hearthwood Log",
  "quest.096D4B6971E6F817.title": "&fShimmerweave Fabric",
  "quest.120CAE5492D8D2FE.quest_desc": [
    "When night falls in a cold biome there is a &b33% chance&r an aurora begins. Any biome tagged as cold counts, such as Snowy Plains, Ice Spikes, Frozen Ocean, Frozen Peaks, Grove and Snowy Taiga.",
    "",
    "While one is running:",
    "- &aGlacial Basins&r fill with Liquid Aura.",
    "- &2Shimmersteel and Shimmerweave&r repair themselves while equipped.",
    "- &aAuroral Nautiluses&r drift in near you.",
    "- &2Aurora Blooms&r appear on snow.",
    "",
    "An aurora lasts anywhere from five minutes to the rest of the night, and it always stops at dawn. Have your basins placed before dark so none of it goes to waste.",
    "",
    "An Aurora Shard is made by infusing Frozen Petals in a basin.",
  ],
  "quest.38EF63D7153D6AC5.quest_desc": [
    "Your primary workstation, and the heart of the whole mod.",
    "",
    "Place it in a &bcold biome&r, wait for an aurora, and watch it fill with &bLiquid Aura&r up to three levels. Then right-click it holding the input. A basin outside a cold biome never fills.",
    "",
    "- &aUnrefined Shimmersteel&r → Shimmersteel Ingot (costs all 3)",
    "- &2Woven Leather&r → Shimmerweave Fabric (1)",
    "- &aFrozen Petals&r → Aurora Shard (1)",
    "- &2Ice&r → Shimmering Ice (1)",
    "",
    "Place several basins. More basins means more aura per event.",
  ],
  "quest.7694FA3E97015D23.title": "&dAurora Blooms",
  "quest.427563F5E92CA507.title": "&5Ender Blooms",
  "quest.4E42490104D43551.title": "&fThe Shimmersteel Bow",
  "quest.6A1048464ABAA02B.title": "&fShimmersteel Ingots",
  "quest.761D8E1A5322E1CB.title": "&6S'nore",
  "quest.455141615CF5D0FC.title": "&bThe Cold Brewing Stand",
  "quest.734BB52B2E3B94D5.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click a &aSnow Golem&r with an &dAurora Shard&r and it turns into an &bAuroral Snowlette&r, a small pet that follows you around. The shard is used up. This works at any time, with or without an aurora.",
    "",
    "It heals when you hit it with a snowball, so keep a few on you.",
  ],
}